/> <br /> As such, it became a popular ghost story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah like people don\u2019t know how absurdly racist America was, (not that racism isn\u2019t a big problem but less so)<br /> <br /> Like after WW2 in the forties where I heard that around 80% or higher % of American Military personal took Japanese \u201cmistresses\u201d and there\u2019s this huge outcry of Asiaitic women polluting the American gene pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:50:46-07:00","id":1411383,"title":"","content":"Lol wut? Source required","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T10:57:12-07:00","id":1411386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1411237-what\u2019s-up-with-our-cultures-fascination-with-the-\u201clost\u201d-colony-of-roanoke?p=1411251#post1411251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic answer seems easy enough:<br /> <br /> US mainstream culture is built on a paradox of wanting to be independent from European culture, while also wanting to be seen as the next step if Western Civilization (aka... being part of European culture).<br /> <br /> As such, mainstream American culture has a long history of sensationalizing anything that can somehow mix American specific cultural elements, while also promoting a sense of moral superiority on the European aspect of things... which is also why white nationalists love this stuff.<br /> <br /> Obsession with events like the Roanoke colony allow the creation of a &amp;quot;unique&amp;quot; American cultural mythology/folk lore without having to cease being a European culture in character.</div> </div> </div> </div>The need for a national mythology is a good explanation for a lot of the weird folklore the US has accumulated in its brief history (did Bigfoot ever get statted in a White Wolf game, or were sightings just chalked up to Delirium affects from werewolf sightings?)<br /> <br /> I've heard it said of Tolkein that The Silmarillion was a similar attempt to create an English myth cycle, since Anglo-Saxon culture doesn't have the deep and ancient roots in the UK that the Scots, the Irish, and the Welsh have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T11:24:51-07:00","id":1411392,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure Bigfoot is in the bygone bestiary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T11:37:53-07:00","id":1411395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1411237-what\u2019s-up-with-our-cultures-fascination-with-the-\u201clost\u201d-colony-of-roanoke?p=1411386#post1411386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The need for a national mythology is a good explanation for a lot of the weird folklore the US has accumulated in its brief history (did Bigfoot ever get statted in a White Wolf game, or were sightings just chalked up to Delirium affects from werewolf sightings?)<br /> <br /> I've heard it said of Tolkein that The Silmarillion was a similar attempt to create an English myth cycle, since Anglo-Saxon culture doesn't have the deep and ancient roots in the UK that the Scots, the Irish, and the Welsh have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bigfoot is a Thallain actually. And yeah Americans are known as desperate for a history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T11:44:11-07:00","id":1411397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1411237-what\u2019s-up-with-our-cultures-fascination-with-the-\u201clost\u201d-colony-of-roanoke?p=1411395#post1411395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bigfoot is a Thallain actually. And yeah Americans are known as desperate for a history.</div> </div> </div> </div>By who exactly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T13:19:27-07:00","id":1411424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1411237-what\u2019s-up-with-our-cultures-fascination-with-the-\u201clost\u201d-colony-of-roanoke?p=1411397#post1411397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By who exactly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stephen King said that this is the basis for the Western in ON WRITING and why he wrote the Dark Tower series. It's also an academic theory that was discussed in my Literature class where Americans attempt to conflate the age of their nation and the Founding Fathers to mythical levels because they are such a young nation.<br /> <br /> The Wild West, Founding Fathers, WW2 movies, Hollywood as a whole, and other ideas being ways the United States attempts to give itself a grandiose history that it frankly doesn't have. America basically overcompensating because it doesn't have a lengthy cultural legacy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T15:00:16-07:00","id":1411438,"title":"","content":"Yeah I dislike Wild West movies for Either praising or ignoring the whole ethnic cleansing, Chinese laborer discrimination, and slavery thing. Plus the whole idea of cowboy having epic gun fights instead of you know herding cows is fake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-01T16:13:18-07:00","id":1411444,"title":"","content":"Well John Ford knew that. The Man who killed Liberty Valance was all about the distance between the mythology of the western and real world.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=363ZAmQEA84\" data-code=\"363ZAmQEA84\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/363ZAmQEA84/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T15:54:08-08:00","id":1429429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1411237-what\u2019s-up-with-our-cultures-fascination-with-the-\u201clost\u201d-colony-of-roanoke?p=1411438#post1411438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I dislike Wild West movies for Either praising or ignoring the whole ethnic cleansing, Chinese laborer discrimination, and slavery thing. Plus the whole idea of cowboy having epic gun fights instead of you know herding cows is fake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of, but the O.K. Corral was real. (Except for the part where the Earp brothers shot the other guys in the back.) But for real, there were lots of small local ranch wars where cowboys did have like one or two big gunfights per war and a bunch of smaller ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T14:32:00-08:00","id":1548501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1411237-what\u2019s-up-with-our-cultures-fascination-with-the-\u201clost\u201d-colony-of-roanoke?p=1411438#post1411438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I dislike Wild West movies for Either praising or ignoring the whole ethnic cleansing, Chinese laborer discrimination, and slavery thing. Plus the whole idea of cowboy having epic gun fights instead of you know herding cows is fake.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true<br /> <br /> The irony being the Wild West was a massive thing for black and Hispanic Americans too.<br /> <br /> But that gets ignored.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-14T18:05:09-08:00","id":1548505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1411237-what\u2019s-up-with-our-cultures-fascination-with-the-\u201clost\u201d-colony-of-roanoke?p=1411438#post1411438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I dislike Wild West movies for Either praising or ignoring the whole ethnic cleansing, Chinese laborer discrimination, and slavery thing. Plus the whole idea of cowboy having epic gun fights instead of you know herding cows is fake.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is kind of funny though because a lot of the things modern day people believe about cowboys (which they got from movies), people back in the 1890's and early 1900's also believed. At the time, journalists would sensationalize stories about cowboys and gunfights, with which a handful of exceptions, weren't really a thing, and publish those stories in books and journals. And then those accounts took hold in the popular consciousness (nevermind that they weren't true). Eventually those stories formed the basis for cowboy movies, which in turn is what most people think the wild west was like. &quot;Journalists&quot; were trying to write stories about the fastest draw in the west to get people to pay them money and stories about discrimination or ethnic cleansing didn't sell and were incredibly hard to find publishers for.<br /> <br /> So what you see (and don't see) involving the &quot;old West&quot; isn't something created wholecloth by Hollywood, but instead it's a series of stories and ideas that started with newspaper writers and journalists of the time period and was simply adopted by people who came later. <br /> <br /> Really, that sort of &quot;yellow journalism&quot; is a bit of a problem, in terms of historical research. A lot of newspapers in the 1860's-1920's were often far, far more interested in sensationalizing the news for profit that in accurately recording what was really happening. So when historical researchers look back into that time period, they have to be a bit more careful in remembering that these sources felt that the truth was of secondary importance to profit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-15T01:54:54-08:00","id":1548510,"title":"","content":"Um, you two realize you're replying to a 4.5 year old post from a banned user... right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-02-15T16:45:41-08:00","id":1548524,"title":"","content":"I'll use this thread to mention,back in the day, I read an alternate-history scenario in which, Japan colonized Western America right before the Europeans did and you had numerous Japanese castles and paper-villages dotting the landscape and thinking, &quot;This would be a great setting for a Kindred of the East or Hengeyokai game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-03T11:54:41-08:00","id":1548915,"title":"","content":"So how did this thread get a second Life?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T09:02:28-08:00","id":1549016,"title":"","content":"In answer to the original question. We as a species love stories, puzzles and mysteries and like to learn more.<br /> <br /> We are curious about what happened to DB Cooper after he parachuted off the plane he held up to get money from the authorities. To this day we don't know what happened to him or most of the money \ud83d\udcb8\ud83d\udcb0.<br /> <br /> With Roanoke we have a colony that vanished without a trace and the only thing they left was the word Croata and that falls under wanting to solve a mystery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-07-2025, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T12:08:41-08:00","id":1549019,"title":"","content":"The problem is when the love of narrative overrides actually learning more; which is unfortunately a side-effect of our species inclinations towards narratives over facts.<br /> <br /> Like, Roanoke Colony isn't really something that inspires a lot of real critical historical study from most people. It's status as a &quot;mystery&quot; is more important to people than the fact that we basically figured out what happened as best as will ever be possible without inventing time travel. The clear answer that the colonists couldn't hold out on their own and turned to the Croatoan people to help isn't &quot;good enough&quot; because it ceases to be an interesting story when you have an answer. People get more wrapped up in what-if stories that don't really care about history because those are fun, than they do start to study what I think plenty of us here consider fascinating in the real nuanced history of the interactions of early European settlers and the indigenous peoples that they interacted with. <br /> <br /> People also don't particularly like the some parts of history are just never going to be known; despite most events in history being forgotten over time anyway. Most people don't even know why we call it the D. B. Cooper case... which was a publishing error by a reporter that misheard the police who related the suspect's alias was Dan Cooper (and there was never any recorded change from Dan Cooper during the incident) that caught on and people gave up trying to correct it because ultimately does it matter what fake name he gave? But why do people really still care? There's two options: the authorities were correct and Cooper died from parachuting in those conditions but those conditions also made finding the body and rest of the money near pointlessly futile, or he got away with it, and with the same attention to detail that went into his plan, had a plan for the money that wasn't spending it (as none of the bills besides a few found in the 80s have ever shown back up in circulation). So basically, the most &quot;exciting&quot; version of events is that he pulled a fairly impressive heist off just to prove that he could, and then disappeared without ever caring about the money and thus didn't spend it so it couldn't be traced back to him; until he would have died of some other cause since otherwise he'd be near 100 years old now.<br /> <br /> Which is all to say that when the intrigue becomes the most important part. The unknowable and unsolvable can become the enemy of learning instead of the friend because they encourage conspiratorial thinking instead of critical thinking, and obsessing over finding clues rather than enjoying the neat stuff you learn along the way of studying the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-06T15:38:20-08:00","id":1549031,"title":"","content":"That is true Heavy Arms. I remember reading about Brush Bill Roberts claiming to be Billy The Kid in 1950. I was skeptical as I couldn't see William Bonny or whatever his real name is could stay out of trouble and not get killed long before dying of old age.<br /> <br /> Or J.M. James being Jesse James and he faked his death and Bob Ford didn't kill him. I also didn't buy into the story as his family was under close watch by the authorities.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough there is some in the FBI that beleived that they found who might be the actual DB Cooper as there was a plane high jacking that was very close to how DB did right down to his appearance and being knowledgeable about parachute jumping and how airplanes work. But it was never really proven.<br /> <br /> Or more recently is the narrative that the reason that Hulk Hogan was booed at WWE house show was that he is a Trump supporter, but overlooking the fact that the Undertaker and Triple H were supporters of the current President and they got cheered when they appeared.<br /> <br /> People have learned over the years that Terry &quot; Hulk Hogan&quot; Bolea is nothing like his wrestling persona and that he screwed a few of his fellow wrestlers over and he likes to tell tall tales or maybe I should say that he has a flexible approach to the truth. So his support for Trump only played a small part of at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation S